{"id": "EUVD-2026-97607", "enisaUuid": "6643ef01-0d64-3432-b53e-bffdbb761699", "description": "Craft CMS from 5.10.2 before 5.10.14 contains a Twig sandbox bypass that allows non-admin users to invoke PHP callables through the \"has some\" and \"has every\" operators. Users with the System Messages permission can supply two-argument callables such as passthru or system in sandboxed templates to execute code as the web user.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:05:59", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/craftcms/cms/security/advisories/GHSA-vfcw-xv8p-8rj2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/craft-cms-5.10.2-before-5.10.14-twig-sandbox-bypass-rce-via-has-some-has-every"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xcjh-qqjq-gq4g", "CVE-2026-109305"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b006f32-67de-30c9-ad0f-ff979061113c", "product": {"name": "CMS", "vendor": {"name": "statamic"}}, "product_version": "5.10.2 <5.10.14"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "12ef0075-ce39-392d-9f83-88f8421db786", "vendor": {"name": "craftcms"}}], "isExploited": false}